      <title>New research and data point to underappreciated risk of fast-moving grassfires</title>
      <link>https://www.kunr.org/2026-02-06/wildfires-grassfires-colorado-idaho-marshall-fire-university-of-colorado-boulder</link>
      <description>Think of the phrase 'The Wildfire Crisis.' What comes to mind? Is it walls of flame marching through pine forests, laying siege to mountain towns? Recent research highlights a different and under-appreciated risk: fast fires racing through dry grass and brush – threatening neighborhoods.</description>
